                <pb facs="0656" n="560" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg560"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/1905: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Clark</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-11-02T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 2,
                                1926—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>30. Your 38 of October 24 and 39 of October 25. The Department has been informed
                    by the Finance Corporation that it possesses absolutely no information
                    concerning the alleged London conference on rubber prices and that no
                    consideration of such a character is influencing the corporation in the
                    negotiations now pending.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
